WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.800
Six questions. One had an answer.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.200
For this one, the code goes first.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.600
The plan was to read bullet lists.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.500
Four real pages put features in headings.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.400
The bullets are the footer.

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.500
Fourteen of them, on one page.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.800
So the parser finds it and the model names it.

8
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.300
Cutting the name is the part that needs a reader.

9
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.400
Then a Basecamp feature showed up at Linear.

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.000
It was the example in our own prompt.

11
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.900
A prompt example is a source with no URL.

12
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.600
Nothing to cite, and nothing to check.

13
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.600
A name cannot be quoted. It can be traced.

14
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.400
Every word of it has to be on the page.

15
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.400
One page had said nothing, in 2,167 words.

16
00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.200
Silence is the failure that looks like an answer.
